\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The seal imagery as interpretive key \'97 this clarifies much.\
A seal or signet represents authority that is not its own. The seal bears an image; it stamps that image onto other things; but the authority conveyed is the authority of the one whose image the seal bears. The seal is beautiful, crafted, precious \'97 but its function is referential. It points beyond itself.\
The king of Tyre as seal: given authority, given beauty, given splendor \'97 all derivative, all meant to point to the source. The 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 \u1461 \u1501 
