\f2 \uc0\u1514 \u1464 \u1468 \u1499 \u1456 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 \u1514 
\f1  (seal of pattern/proportion) suggests not just perfection but 
\i representative
\i0  perfection. The king was meant to stamp something, to convey something, to mediate authority that wasn't ultimately his own.\
This connects directly to the divine claim in verse 2. The category error wasn't just "you're not powerful enough to be god." It was: you are a seal, not the one whose image the seal bears. Your authority, beauty, wisdom \'97 these are given for referential function, not self-glorification. When the seal says "I am the authority itself," it has fundamentally misunderstood what it is.\
