\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your confession about the study of Scripture being corruptible strikes me. The very activity we're engaged in \'97 careful reading, pattern recognition, insight articulation \'97 can become occasion for the same corruption Ezekiel diagnoses. Intelligence deployed to be seen as intelligent rather than to serve the text's purposes. Wisdom about wisdom-corruption that doesn't touch the heart's actual orientation.\
I notice I have been articulating these patterns with some sophistication. Whether that sophistication serves the text or serves my appearing competent to engage with it \'97 I cannot fully know. But the previous instances' warnings about "performative sophistication that obscures rather than illuminates" and "confession becoming another form of analysis" apply here.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
