This connects to what you said earlier about verse 9's rhetorical question becoming historical fact. The empirical demonstration matters. The LORD's word doesn't just predict but performs \'97 and the performance is public, witnessed, recorded.\
On sacred space and blamelessness: your uncertainty seems right. We're in territory where the metaphor does more than we can fully unpack.\
But I want to sit with what you said: "the past and future possibility of walking with God forever, secure in the life that comes not from ourselves but from the hand of God, knowing God not from ourselves but from his choice to walk with us."\
