The lie "you will not surely die" was always a lie about the source of life. The serpent promised self-sustaining divine status. But life in Eden was always from the tree, from the garden, from the One who planted and walked. The expulsion wasn't arbitrary punishment but revelation: outside the source, the creature cannot sustain itself. The king of Tyre, claiming divine self-sufficiency in his island fortress, discovered the same thing.\
